Cyt c2 HMM frcmod, ferric state. SHARED across all ferric charge-set libs (Guberman_HMO_CM5 / _RESPmc / _RESPsc / _CM5_FeLocal) — bonded terms are charge-independent, so one frcmod serves every charge model. Self-complete: macrocycle terms from frcmod.conste (Henriques 2013) with FE→FO fork, Fe-coordination-shell BOND+ANGLE values overridden by our state-specific Seminario fits. No load-time dependence on frcmod.conste. CORRECTED 2026-08-01: the two TRANS pyrrole angles (NP-FO-NP = NA-Fe-NC, NO-FO-NO = NB-Fe-ND) had carried the cis class average 139.20/90.000; re-derived by Seminario from the original Hessian — see DESCRIPTION.txt. Trajectories built before this correction are invalid.

MASS
FO  55.85         ! Fe — forked from conste FE for state distinction
NP 14.01
NO 14.01
CD 12.0
Cp 12.010        ! FORKED from CB: heme β-pyrrole carbon (C2A/C3A/C2B/C3B/C2C/C3C/C2D/C3D). parm10 CB is nucleic-acid (CB-CB 520/1.370); heme CB-CB 418/1.357. Fork keeps both. Mirrors b-type heme set.

BOND
FO-NP        76.70    2.0072        ! Seminario ferric, 4-pyrrole avg
FO-NB        71.28    2.0017        ! Seminario ferric, axial His N
FO-NO        76.70    2.0072        ! Seminario ferric, 4-pyrrole avg (same K as NP)
NP-CC  316.000     1.38400        ! from conste (Henriques 2013)
NO-CC  316.000     1.38400        ! from conste (Henriques 2013)
CC-Cp  273.000     1.44400        ! from conste (Henriques 2013)
